Triangle $ABC$ has vertices $A(1,2)$, $B(3,2)$, $C(1,5)$. It is reflected in the $y$-axis. What are the coordinates of $A'$, $B'$ and $C'$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.5]
\draw[step=1,gray!25,very thin] (-5,-5) grid (5,5);
\draw[<->,thick] (-5.5,0)--(5.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->,thick] (0,-5.5)--(0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-5,-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5} \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {-5,-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5} \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,\y) {$\y$};
\draw[thick] (1,2)--(3,2)--(1,5)--cycle;
\fill (1,2) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below right,font=\footnotesize] at (1,2) {$A$};
\fill (3,2) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below right,font=\footnotesize] at (3,2) {$B$};
\fill (1,5) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above right,font=\footnotesize] at (1,5) {$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The point $B(4,1)$ is mapped to its image $B'(-1,4)$ by a single transformation about the origin. Which transformation is it?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.5]
\draw[step=1,gray!25,very thin] (-5,-5) grid (5,5);
\draw[<->,thick] (-5.5,0)--(5.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->,thick] (0,-5.5)--(0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-5,-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5} \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {-5,-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5} \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,\y) {$\y$};
\fill (4,1) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below right,font=\footnotesize] at (4,1) {$B$};
\draw[fill=white] (-1,4) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above left,font=\footnotesize] at (-1,4) {$B'$};
\draw[dashed,gray] (0,0)--(4,1);
\draw[dashed,gray] (0,0)--(-1,4);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

